kirby in the forgotten land is the pink  puffball's biggest game yet it has more  moving parts to keep track of than its  predecessors and it also happens to be  the trickiest entry from a puzzle and  combat perspective while the forgotten  land is still fairly straightforward  there are some tricks of the trade we  picked up throughout our time with the  game and we've rounded up 10 tips and  tricks for kirby and the forgotten land  if you like this kind of video and want  to see more then consider subscribing to  gamespot  each level has a batch of waddle dees to  find a few are earned simply by beating  the level and every level outside of  boss stages has several hidden waddle  dees but each level also has three or  four other hidden objectives if you take  your time exploring each stage carefully  you should be able to uncover a secret  or two or perhaps even all of them in  one go complete the hidden objectives  and you'll free additional waddle dee's  if you don't find the secret objectives  though and some are really well hidden  so don't beat yourself up over it you  will have a better chance the next time  each time you complete a level one of  the mystery objectives will reveal  itself essentially this is a brief  statement that describes the objective  it can hint to a secret room or a poster  that needs to be knocked down or even a  group of ducks that needs to be reunited  with their mama once you have the clue  it should be easier to be on the lookout  the next time you play through the stage  kirby's copy ability has been his  signature move for decades so it's no  surprise that it's vitally important in  kirby in the forgotten land not only do  copy abilities help kirby in combat but  they are often required to solve puzzles  and levels to help find waddle dees  if there are enemies nearby that have a  specific ability drill fire tornado  cutter hammer there's a good chance a  puzzle or secret area that requires that  ability is around the corner if you're  going through entire levels with the  same ability chances are you're missing  some secrets  it's also worth noting that copy  abilities won't show up in the weapon  shop in waddle d-town until you use them  at least once so they're worth sucking  up for that reason too  kirby in the forgotten land revolves  around cool abilities that turn kirby  into a wrecking ball of force especially  when you upgrade those copy abilities  but it can be easy to forget that kirby  also has a built-in defense mechanism if  you're having trouble with a boss some  of the later ones can definitely be  tricky you're probably not playing  defense in spots where you could kirby's  guard ability can help mitigate damage  so watch your enemies moveset and put up  your guard the next time the brute tries  to hit you while the game doesn't  explicitly explain guarding you can use  any of the triggers or shoulder buttons  to guard so l zl r and zr and all of  them perform the same guard move you can  also move the control stick while  guarding to do a cool dodge move  [Music]  not long into the game you'll rescue  enough waddle dee's to have a house  built in waddle dee town this small  dome-shaped building is kind of plain  but it does serve a great purpose  kirby starts each level with the same  amount of health he had at the end of  the last so depending on how the  previous level went for you that could  mean trouble but you can take a trip  back to waddle d-town and rest in  kirby's bed to replenish your health bar  if you have any amiibo you can use them  to get in-game items in kirby in the  forgotten land amiibo not related to the  kirby franchise drops some coins and a  piece of fruit that replenishes health  if you do have kirby themed amiibo each  one does a different thing that could  prove to be helpful the boost and health  items you receive by scanning amiibo can  be used once and have a temporary effect  so scanning the kirby amiibo gives you a  life up which doubles your health as  well as star coins scanning the meta  knight amiibo gives you a speed boost as  well as start coins king dedede an  attack boost and coins and then waddle d  gives you a health potion and coins  nintendo recently reprinted the kirby  series kirby and meta knight amiibo as  well as the smash bros king dedede  amiibo for the release of this game so  some of the amiibo listed above should  be available in stores and online if  you're looking to try this out  you can also buy the previously  mentioned boost once the item shop opens  in the top right corner of waddle d-town  these boots can be very useful towards  the end of the game or if you're playing  co-op alongside someone who isn't very  familiar with action platformers  attack and speed boost can be stacked up  to five times plus you can hold the  sixth each boost lasts for 200 seconds  so if you add up all five it's a  thousand seconds  boost can be really helpful for the  coliseum which is essentially a boss  rush mode that can get pretty  challenging meanwhile health items can  be purchased at the wattle d cafe before  the item shop even opens  while the cafe serves several different  items we'd recommend sticking to the  maxim tomato since it only costs 100  coins and restores all of your health  you can carry one item or boost with you  at a time so it's helpful to always have  a maximum tomato on hand just in case  [Music]  often times before boss fights you get  to pick a copy ability to equip this is  the copy ability you'll be stuck with  for the whole battle so it's good to  stick with abilities you're used to but  if you have to choose between an evolved  ability and an ability that's still in  its standard state it's smart to go with  the evolved ability to deal more damage  if the copy ability you want to use  isn't available in that level you can  head to the weapon shop and equip your  favorite ability before entering the  boss level  some boss attack patterns don't gel with  the copy ability you're using in these  cases it doesn't hurt to drop the copy  ability and kill the boss the  old-fashioned way by sucking up and  shooting stars at them plus if you're  quick and you manage to inhale multiple  stars at once you can wind up doing more  damage than unevolved copy abilities  try to charge up your sword or hammer or  any of the copy abilities while fighting  a boss and look to see how much damage  you're doing you can do this by holding  b by default or y if you change your  controller settings there's a stark  difference between charged attacks and  regular hits this becomes even more  pronounced as you evolve your abilities  evolve forms or charge attacks can also  hinder enemy movement and give you even  more opportunities to deal damage i  found charge attacks of evolve fire and  ice abilities to be the most effective  seriously they are wild  [Applause]  [Music]  treasure road levels unlock as you  complete mainline missions  these time trials challenge you to use  one copy ability or mouthful mode as  efficiently as possible they are pretty  straightforward but here are a few  important details to know  first we recommend completing all of the  treasure road levels in a world before  moving on to the next world's mainline  missions this is because the rare stones  you acquire by completing them allow you  to evolve your copy abilities  second don't worry about the target time  of each level this secondary objective  only nets you a bonus of 50 coins so  there's not much of a point to try over  and over again to hit that time  especially when the target time tends to  require a near perfect run and lastly  explore the overworld carefully there  are a few points of interest usually  areas that look like something should be  there that prompt you to press a to  search the area some treasure road  levels are hidden and do not reveal  themselves until you unearth them this  way  and there you have it 10 things to get  you started in kirby and the forgotten  land  for more on kirby in the forgotten land  be sure to check out our review by  stephen petit both here on our youtube  channel as well as our website  gamespot.com we also have a written  version of this exact guide on our  website as well  and hey thank you so much for watching  for all things kirby and nintendo stay  tuned to gamespot  do  [Music]  you
 

